1
00:00:00,173 --> 00:00:03,133
Bakit nga ba hindi reliable ang somatotypes?

2
00:00:03,373 --> 00:00:06,533
Mainly ectomorph, endomorph, and mesomorph?

3
00:00:06,827 --> 00:00:07,827
Here's the reality.

4
00:00:08,067 --> 00:00:11,167
Somatotypes aren't rooted in modern exercise science.

5
00:00:11,427 --> 00:00:13,247
Inimbento 'to noong 1940s

6
00:00:13,287 --> 00:00:16,547
ng isang psychologist named William Herbert Sheldon.

7
00:00:16,887 --> 00:00:19,667
And get this, hindi man lang fitness o metabolism

8
00:00:19,667 --> 00:00:20,727
ang pinag-aralan niya.

9
00:00:20,987 --> 00:00:24,467
He used constitutional psychology para subukang patunayan

10
00:00:24,707 --> 00:00:27,487
na your body shape dictates your personality

11
00:00:27,947 --> 00:00:30,027
intelligence, and tendencies sa delinquency.

12
00:00:31,927 --> 00:00:34,947
Modern exercise physiology has debunked this over and over.

13
00:00:35,047 --> 00:00:38,047
Ang katawan natin is polygenic at infinitely

14
00:00:38,047 --> 00:00:41,467
more complex kaysa sa three arbitrary boxes.

15
00:00:41,707 --> 00:00:44,047
Somatotype isn't a genetic blueprint.

16
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:47,027
It's a snapshot of your current energy balance,

17
00:00:47,127 --> 00:00:48,467
muscle mass, and lifestyle.

18
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:53,413
Ectomorph ako kaya hindi ako masyado nagkakalaman?

19
00:00:53,493 --> 00:00:56,453
Or endomorph ako kaya doomed na akong tumaba?

20
00:00:56,573 --> 00:01:00,273
You are not trapped in a label made in the 1940s.

21
00:01:00,493 --> 00:01:01,313
Control your nutrition,

22
00:01:01,413 --> 00:01:04,873
train hard and stop capping your own potential.
